1
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:06,173
[toilet flushing]

2
00:00:08,675 --> 00:00:10,219
[Satoshi breathes heavily]

3
00:00:10,302 --> 00:00:15,057
The reason I applied
is because I'm interested in advertising.

4
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:17,017
[stomach growling]

5
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:18,894
[groans] Maybe restroom again?

6
00:00:18,977 --> 00:00:21,897
It's Kyobashi, right? You gotta hurry.

7
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:24,691
What if I have diarrhea
on the train today?

8
00:00:24,942 --> 00:00:27,444
No diarrhea allowed on any day.

9
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:32,950
Chiko, you need to be more serious.

10
00:00:33,909 --> 00:00:35,202
What did you say?

11
00:00:35,285 --> 00:00:37,246
[Satoshi] Oh, my bag.

12
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:45,712
-[sighs]
-[door opens]

13
00:01:04,314 --> 00:01:05,941
[indistinct chatter]

14
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:09,361
[employee] Yes, of course.
Thanks, I'm counting on you.

15
00:01:15,367 --> 00:01:17,786
-[stomach growling]
-[groans]

16
00:01:17,869 --> 00:01:22,249
RED LIGHT ELEGY

17
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:24,918
-[knocking on door]
-[employee] Boss.

18
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:27,045
-The applicant is here.
-[employer] Okay.

19
00:01:27,129 --> 00:01:28,130
Just get inside.

20
00:01:28,213 --> 00:01:30,340
-Pardon me.
-[employer] Come on in.

21
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:32,884
Come sit here.

22
00:01:51,361 --> 00:01:53,989
-A female?
-Huh?

23
00:01:56,908 --> 00:01:58,035
You're a female.

24
00:01:58,785 --> 00:02:00,537
Can't females apply here?

25
00:02:05,042 --> 00:02:06,209
[employer] It's male here.

26
00:02:07,836 --> 00:02:10,005
-[gasps]
-[♪ tense music playing]

27
00:02:10,881 --> 00:02:12,966
Wait... Excuse me!

28
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:23,852
-[staff] Next person, please.
-[interviewee 1] Yes!

29
00:02:30,817 --> 00:02:33,195
I wanna take a call.

30
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:36,198
I'm up to here now. Can you hold my spot?

31
00:02:36,281 --> 00:02:37,783
[line ringing]

32
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:46,708
[interviewee 2] Hey, bro, it's your turn.

33
00:02:48,251 --> 00:02:49,503
Got it.

34
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:52,005
[knocking on door]

35
00:02:53,048 --> 00:02:54,716
-The applicant is coming.
-[interviewer] Okay.

36
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:56,093
Pardon me.

37
00:02:56,510 --> 00:02:58,387
[interviewer]
Hand in your résumé and be seated.

38
00:02:59,179 --> 00:03:01,181
Well... Actually, I...

39
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:03,934
Can you hurry up? People are waiting.

40
00:03:04,226 --> 00:03:06,353
[Satoshi] I'm sorry.

41
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:11,024
Well... Actually...

42
00:03:12,234 --> 00:03:13,819
[hurried footsteps approaching]

43
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:15,112
This one!

44
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:17,447
Chiko! What are you doing here?

45
00:03:17,531 --> 00:03:18,949
Whatever.

46
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:22,411
-What about your interview?
-Idiot. Focus on yours.

47
00:03:23,537 --> 00:03:25,956
-[Chiko] I'm leaving.
-[Satoshi] Thanks...

48
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:27,374
Thanks a lot!

49
00:03:29,167 --> 00:03:30,252
[sighs]

50
00:03:32,379 --> 00:03:35,966
Can we just start our interview?

51
00:03:38,510 --> 00:03:39,761
Yes!

52
00:03:45,058 --> 00:03:46,852
Let's do it.

53
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:49,354
I'm ready.

54
00:03:51,273 --> 00:03:54,484
Can we start with why you applied here?

55
00:03:54,568 --> 00:03:55,861
Yes!

56
00:03:55,944 --> 00:03:59,698
To begin with,
I've always enjoyed watching commercials.

57
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:02,117
[sighs]

58
00:04:11,710 --> 00:04:13,211
[line ringing]

59
00:04:17,424 --> 00:04:19,885
Hello. This is Akiyama speaking.

60
00:04:20,677 --> 00:04:22,053
Yes, I am.

61
00:04:22,763 --> 00:04:24,639
I'm sorry for the trouble.

62
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:27,434
Yes. Well...

63
00:04:29,352 --> 00:04:30,395
What?

64
00:04:30,479 --> 00:04:31,688
Boring.

65
00:04:32,773 --> 00:04:36,526
Everything I read and hear
just flow right past me.

66
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:38,612
Well...

67
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:42,991
[interviewer] You're just repeating
what you read, right?

68
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:45,535
[scoffs] That's so obvious.

69
00:04:45,619 --> 00:04:47,120
No, I just--

70
00:04:47,204 --> 00:04:49,122
[interviewer] What are your strengths?

71
00:04:49,539 --> 00:04:52,209
-Guess you only know your weaknesses.
-[stomach growling]

72
00:04:52,876 --> 00:04:54,461
If you don't look ahead

73
00:04:54,544 --> 00:04:57,839
and brace yourself to ride out
the rough waves of this world,

74
00:04:58,381 --> 00:05:00,383
-you end up like you.
-[♪ tense music playing]

75
00:05:00,467 --> 00:05:04,262
-Don't you ever think about your future?
-[rumbling continues]

76
00:05:05,847 --> 00:05:07,849
No, I--

77
00:05:07,933 --> 00:05:11,603
That delinquent chick is your girl, right?

78
00:05:12,062 --> 00:05:14,606
Those people just live aimlessly.

79
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:18,235
Then they have kids recklessly

80
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:20,821
-and waste social welfare.
-[♪ tense music continues]

81
00:05:21,446 --> 00:05:23,824
Who'd want to pay taxes for them?

82
00:05:26,827 --> 00:05:28,662
Chiko is a good girl!

83
00:05:29,371 --> 00:05:34,251
Isn't judging people you don't know
making the world even worse?

84
00:05:36,378 --> 00:05:38,213
Well, well, well.

85
00:05:39,756 --> 00:05:42,425
Now you can speak out in your own words

86
00:05:43,844 --> 00:05:45,887
despite failing the interview.

87
00:05:49,099 --> 00:05:51,685
I'll live a happy life with Chiko.

88
00:05:51,768 --> 00:05:55,689
That's way better,
and that's why I'm getting a job.

89
00:05:56,231 --> 00:05:57,399
So long!

90
00:06:03,697 --> 00:06:05,740
Hey, how was it?

91
00:06:07,367 --> 00:06:12,414
No way, I completely blew it.
I took job hunting too lightly.

92
00:06:13,290 --> 00:06:16,126
Sorry, after all your trouble
bringing my résumé.

93
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:17,544
Not at all.

94
00:06:18,837 --> 00:06:20,422
How about you?

95
00:06:21,965 --> 00:06:24,509
Well...

96
00:06:25,635 --> 00:06:27,846
I'm hired.

97
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:31,141
What? Really? That's great!

98
00:06:32,350 --> 00:06:34,436
-Wow!
-Are you all right?

99
00:06:34,978 --> 00:06:38,648
I'm fine.
I'm not gonna let one failure get me down!

100
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:42,611
Right? Now let's celebrate Chiko first!

101
00:06:42,694 --> 00:06:44,487
Do it at home.

102
00:06:44,988 --> 00:06:46,197
I'll grab some beers.

103
00:06:46,990 --> 00:06:48,992
-Congrats!
-Okay.

104
00:06:54,748 --> 00:06:57,834
-[employer] Good morning.
-Good morning.

105
00:06:59,044 --> 00:07:00,337
Shall we go now?

106
00:07:07,677 --> 00:07:10,472
Let's start with learning
the delivery routes.

107
00:07:10,555 --> 00:07:11,598
[Chiko] Got it.

108
00:07:12,932 --> 00:07:18,063
You'll have company at first,
then you'll drive solo once you're set.

109
00:07:18,146 --> 00:07:19,356
[Chiko] Understood.

110
00:07:21,024 --> 00:07:22,859
[engine starts]

111
00:07:32,285 --> 00:07:33,620
All right!

112
00:07:34,371 --> 00:07:35,705
Then, off I go.

113
00:07:35,789 --> 00:07:37,290
Take care of yourself.

114
00:07:37,707 --> 00:07:38,875
See you.

115
00:08:02,899 --> 00:08:03,983
[sighs]

116
00:08:10,573 --> 00:08:12,575
[store owner] <i>"Extremely clumsy," huh?</i>

117
00:08:12,659 --> 00:08:15,662
Cooking is all about hand skills.

118
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:18,957
It's hard to hire someone
with a résumé like this.

119
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:22,877
You need to speak more clearly
if you work in service.

120
00:08:29,342 --> 00:08:32,220
Sales is all about hands-on practice.

121
00:08:32,637 --> 00:08:34,264
Shall we try the practical test?

122
00:08:35,265 --> 00:08:37,267
-Yes.
-[doorbell chimes]

123
00:08:37,809 --> 00:08:39,227
[resident] Coming.

124
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:44,357
Yes, who's this?

125
00:08:44,441 --> 00:08:47,694
Well, we're giving this air purifier free

126
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:51,614
to anyone who signs up to test it.

127
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:54,534
-Here you are.
-Oh...

128
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:56,828
Wait, it's free?

129
00:08:56,911 --> 00:08:58,038
Yes.

130
00:08:59,330 --> 00:09:01,833
But you have to buy the filter
for 10,000 yen.

131
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:04,044
What's that? [scoffs]

132
00:09:04,127 --> 00:09:06,087
-Don't mess with me!
-Huh?

133
00:09:06,171 --> 00:09:09,007
-You're a scammer, aren't you?
-A scammer?

134
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:11,134
[resident]
Aren't you ashamed of selling like this?

135
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:12,427
No, no. I'm not a scam--

136
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:14,846
[resident]
Anyway, the old guy in that room...

137
00:09:16,389 --> 00:09:17,474
[door opens]

138
00:09:17,807 --> 00:09:19,017
[Chiko] I'm back.

139
00:09:19,642 --> 00:09:20,769
[door closes]

140
00:09:26,483 --> 00:09:27,901
Failed again today?

141
00:09:29,235 --> 00:09:30,236
[Satoshi] Yeah.

142
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:39,996
You got scared and panicked again, right?

143
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:44,000
Just talk big,
saying you'd die for this job!

144
00:09:47,087 --> 00:09:48,338
[Satoshi sighs]

145
00:09:50,215 --> 00:09:54,594
[Satoshi] People do die working,
just like my dad.

146
00:09:55,762 --> 00:09:58,348
-Uh...
-[Satoshi sighs]

147
00:09:59,933 --> 00:10:02,435
-Sorry.
-Off to the convenience store.

148
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:07,565
-[door opens]
-[breathing heavily]

149
00:10:09,818 --> 00:10:10,985
[door closes]

150
00:10:13,488 --> 00:10:16,157
[♪ pensive music playing]

151
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:47,981
Well, you'll do.

152
00:10:51,526 --> 00:10:52,569
Yes?

153
00:10:53,611 --> 00:10:54,863
[Satoshi] Thank you so much.

154
00:11:09,419 --> 00:11:10,420
[grunts]

155
00:11:16,217 --> 00:11:18,970
-[phone beeping]
-[indistinct chatter]

156
00:11:36,154 --> 00:11:38,573
-Excuse me.
-[seller] Welcome!

157
00:11:39,991 --> 00:11:41,367
Get me the prime cuts.

158
00:11:41,451 --> 00:11:42,827
[seller] Prime cuts? Sure!

159
00:11:43,536 --> 00:11:44,954
Get the pricy stuff.

160
00:11:45,038 --> 00:11:48,499
[seller] Pricy stuff. All right.
Premium meat!

161
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:51,002
[♪ soft bright music playing]

162
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:08,186
[sighs]

163
00:12:13,816 --> 00:12:18,738
Hey, you! It's you.
What the hell are you thinking?

164
00:12:19,155 --> 00:12:21,157
Man, you're way too drunk.

165
00:12:22,242 --> 00:12:26,871
The manager wants to call it a day.

166
00:12:26,955 --> 00:12:28,122
[chuckles]

167
00:12:32,085 --> 00:12:37,799
What? You looking down on me? [laughs]

168
00:12:37,882 --> 00:12:39,926
Yusaku-kun, knock it off.

169
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:43,137
[drunk] Hey, just say something.

170
00:12:43,221 --> 00:12:46,057
What? You wanna fight?

171
00:12:46,849 --> 00:12:52,146
All size, no fight. Hey, come on. [laughs]

172
00:12:54,065 --> 00:12:56,776
-[store owner] Yusaku-kun, stop it!
-[customers yelp]

173
00:12:58,736 --> 00:12:59,862
[drunk groans]

174
00:13:00,863 --> 00:13:02,073
[drunk] That hurts!

175
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:04,867
[breathing heavily, angrily]

176
00:13:04,951 --> 00:13:06,536
[Chiko] <i>Let go of me!</i>

177
00:13:07,370 --> 00:13:09,706
-[grunts]
-[Yusaku breathing heavily, angrily]

178
00:13:12,667 --> 00:13:14,335
Yu... Yusaku.

179
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:49,912
Chiko...

180
00:13:51,789 --> 00:13:55,209
[soft groan] Just finished it, right?

181
00:13:59,964 --> 00:14:02,383
I'm too nervous to sleep.

182
00:14:03,009 --> 00:14:07,388
I've never touched a computer.
Am I gonna make it?

183
00:14:10,016 --> 00:14:11,017
[sighs]

184
00:14:13,061 --> 00:14:15,146
What kind of a company?

185
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:16,481
Making websites.

186
00:14:16,564 --> 00:14:17,940
What kind?

187
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:24,697
Websites are websites! Using a computer.

188
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:28,826
Don't you know what your company does?

189
00:14:30,078 --> 00:14:34,123
It's fine, it looked like a real office.

190
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:36,709
Is that so?

191
00:14:40,046 --> 00:14:42,256
[whines] Chiko...

192
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:43,883
Give it a rest!

193
00:14:46,844 --> 00:14:48,429
[gasping]

194
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:52,183
Right on the mark.

195
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:54,018
[Chiko] Who cares? Just sleep.

196
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:00,900
-This is good.
-[employee] Right?

197
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:04,529
The pictures we've got here...

198
00:15:04,612 --> 00:15:07,031
[indistinct chatter]

199
00:15:07,115 --> 00:15:09,534
A nice one, right?

200
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:10,618
PACKED WITH HOTTIES!

201
00:15:10,701 --> 00:15:14,831
[manager] "Japan Nightlife Chronicle".
You and Hikasa-kun are taking on this.

202
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:18,960
The rest do foodie blogs
and all sorts of sites,

203
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:21,754
but adult content pays the best.

204
00:15:22,213 --> 00:15:25,258
It's the backbone of our company.

205
00:15:26,717 --> 00:15:30,388
Cover her face well
so her identity stays hidden.

206
00:15:31,097 --> 00:15:32,390
And then...

207
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:35,309
retouch this girl's blemishes.

208
00:15:35,768 --> 00:15:39,939
This girl has so much hair sticking out.

209
00:15:40,273 --> 00:15:41,649
Erase all.

210
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:45,570
I have a few requests,
so just edit the photos based on those.

211
00:15:45,653 --> 00:15:47,780
[employee] Mr. Nakazono,
time for the meeting.

212
00:15:47,864 --> 00:15:48,990
Okay!

213
00:15:49,824 --> 00:15:51,617
Follow the manual and try.

214
00:15:53,286 --> 00:15:55,913
-Hikasa-kun, we have guests today.
-Got it!

215
00:15:56,539 --> 00:15:58,124
[curtain rattling]

216
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:02,420
-[employee] This is what we discussed...
-[Nakazono] Right.

217
00:16:05,798 --> 00:16:07,300
-[customer] The last one?
-[Chiko's colleague] Yes.

218
00:16:08,926 --> 00:16:09,969
[customer] And what?

219
00:16:10,052 --> 00:16:12,138
-Is this lady in charge?
-[Chiko's colleague] Yes.

220
00:16:12,221 --> 00:16:14,390
I'm starting long-haul routes tomorrow.

221
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:19,854
Well, a woman is fine.

222
00:16:20,563 --> 00:16:22,273
As long as she's punctual.

223
00:16:23,024 --> 00:16:24,317
I'll do my best.

224
00:16:33,701 --> 00:16:35,786
[Chiko's colleague] That's not even late.

225
00:16:38,497 --> 00:16:41,834
-Don't sweat it.
-All right, I don't.

226
00:16:43,753 --> 00:16:45,421
-[Chiko's colleague 1] Thanks for today.
-[employer] Thanks.

227
00:16:46,714 --> 00:16:48,132
[employer] Settling in?

228
00:16:48,216 --> 00:16:49,800
Well, kind of.

229
00:16:55,932 --> 00:16:56,933
[Chiko's colleague 2] Hello.

230
00:17:09,904 --> 00:17:16,786
TAMAHIME. ALL FOR LOVE.

231
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:36,180
What the hell are you looking at, idiot?

232
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:38,683
[tuts, yells]

233
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:39,850
[exclaims]

234
00:17:40,351 --> 00:17:44,063
No way! She's actually so cute!

235
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:46,274
I think this is his girlfriend.

236
00:17:46,357 --> 00:17:47,525
[Nakazono] Girlfriend?

237
00:17:47,608 --> 00:17:49,777
-[Hikasa] Cute, right?
-Cute.

238
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,862
This type is the best.

239
00:17:51,946 --> 00:17:53,197
[Satoshi's colleague 1] The best?

240
00:17:53,281 --> 00:17:54,782
Not the best choice, huh?

241
00:17:54,865 --> 00:17:57,159
-[Hikasa] Which one is it?
-[chuckles] What a match.

242
00:17:57,243 --> 00:18:00,413
That's so unfair. Let's drink!

243
00:18:00,496 --> 00:18:02,248
Drink, just drink.

244
00:18:02,331 --> 00:18:05,710
It's on the boss today, so drink up!

245
00:18:05,793 --> 00:18:06,919
[Nakazono] Go for it.

246
00:18:08,879 --> 00:18:10,590
-Wonderful.
-[clapping]

247
00:18:10,673 --> 00:18:12,425
[Satoshi's colleague 2]
Hikasa, drink up too.

248
00:18:12,508 --> 00:18:13,634
[Hikasa] I'll drink then.

249
00:18:13,718 --> 00:18:16,262
Oh, for real.

250
00:18:17,305 --> 00:18:18,431
Well...

251
00:18:19,599 --> 00:18:22,977
Nice that your girl lets you do this job.

252
00:18:23,853 --> 00:18:26,105
Well, actually...

253
00:18:26,772 --> 00:18:28,482
Wait, you haven't told her yet?

254
00:18:28,566 --> 00:18:30,109
Not yet.

255
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:32,028
I wasn't too sure myself.

256
00:18:34,655 --> 00:18:37,658
All because Mr. Nakazono hadn't told you.

257
00:18:38,618 --> 00:18:40,620
You looked committed to this.

258
00:18:41,579 --> 00:18:44,582
There's no escape
once you enter the sex industry.

259
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:50,296
But you can still give it your all.

260
00:18:51,881 --> 00:18:54,675
You're not doing bad things at all.

261
00:18:55,968 --> 00:18:58,137
I'd be fine if I were your girlfriend.

262
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:04,602
[Satoshi's colleague 1] Oh,
Kubocchi has a crush on the new guy!

263
00:19:04,685 --> 00:19:06,562
[Kubocchi] No, that's not it!

264
00:19:06,646 --> 00:19:10,024
-Trust me, rookie. Choose Kubocchi!
-What?

265
00:19:10,107 --> 00:19:11,942
You two make a good pair.

266
00:19:12,026 --> 00:19:13,361
-[Kubocchi] Sorry?
-[Satoshi's colleague 1] This girl...

267
00:19:13,444 --> 00:19:15,571
has never been with a guy at all.

268
00:19:15,655 --> 00:19:18,699
-So please!
-Hold on, what are you talking about?

269
00:19:18,783 --> 00:19:21,452
You're down because you know
it's a sex site, right?

270
00:19:21,535 --> 00:19:23,162
-I know it.
-[Nakazono] Really?

271
00:19:23,245 --> 00:19:24,747
If you wanna quit,

272
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:28,876
you might as well get a new girl first.

273
00:19:28,959 --> 00:19:30,461
[Kubocchi] That's alcohol hazing! Enough!

274
00:19:30,544 --> 00:19:34,298
Well, I'll do my best at this job!

275
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:39,679
[all exclaim]

276
00:19:39,762 --> 00:19:42,348
-Nice!
-[indistinct chatter]

277
00:19:42,431 --> 00:19:43,849
Face off, face off!

278
00:19:43,933 --> 00:19:44,934
Get ready.

279
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:46,811
-Do or die, Akiyama!
-Go for it!

280
00:19:46,894 --> 00:19:48,187
Relax, relax.

281
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:50,940
[Chiko's colleague 1]
All right. Ready... Go!

282
00:19:51,023 --> 00:19:52,817
[Chiko's colleagues cheering] Go!

283
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:54,944
Don't give up!

284
00:19:55,027 --> 00:19:58,989
My, you're still just a mama's girl!

285
00:19:59,073 --> 00:20:02,451
Wonder if you're even a challenge.

286
00:20:02,535 --> 00:20:06,497
-Shut up, old lady!
-[excited cheering]

287
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:07,790
[thuds]

288
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:10,334
[shouting] Yes!

289
00:20:11,043 --> 00:20:13,963
-[Chiko's colleague 2] Ms. Tamayo rules!
-Damn it!

290
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:15,965
[laughs]

291
00:20:16,507 --> 00:20:19,218
-Bring it on anytime!
-[groans]

292
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:21,929
Not gonna lie, you've got real guts.

293
00:20:22,513 --> 00:20:25,349
I heard you wanna do long-haul routes.

294
00:20:25,975 --> 00:20:28,227
-Kind of.
-Hell yeah!

295
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:30,396
[laughs]

296
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:33,399
-I love it!
-[bell jingling]

297
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:36,861
Even so,

298
00:20:36,944 --> 00:20:41,323
it is a lonely job, hitting endless,

299
00:20:41,407 --> 00:20:43,367
brutal roads all by yourself.

300
00:20:44,702 --> 00:20:46,454
You won't see your guy

301
00:20:46,537 --> 00:20:50,166
-or your family for days.
-[Chiko's colleague 1] Right.

302
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:51,792
Better be ready for that.

303
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,837
I'm all good.

304
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:57,131
That's the spirit! Good!

305
00:20:58,382 --> 00:20:59,759
Still,

306
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:05,431
loneliness hits hard as you age.

307
00:21:06,265 --> 00:21:09,894
Just think about that... carefully!

308
00:21:09,977 --> 00:21:12,646
Ouch... That hurts, you old bitch!

309
00:21:12,730 --> 00:21:14,899
[Tamayo] Shut up, you little brat!

310
00:21:17,359 --> 00:21:18,694
[phone vibrating]

311
00:21:24,658 --> 00:21:25,826
Hi.

312
00:21:27,328 --> 00:21:29,580
[Satoshi slurring] <i>Hi, Chiko.</i>

313
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:31,665
You're totally drunk.

314
00:21:32,082 --> 00:21:34,168
[Satoshi] <i>I'm totally fine.</i>

315
00:21:34,251 --> 00:21:36,003
-[Satoshi's phone thuds]
-[Kubocchi yelps]

316
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:38,130
[Satoshi] <i>Ms. Kubo...</i>

317
00:21:38,631 --> 00:21:40,674
[Satoshi's colleague 1]
<i>Ah, Kubocchi is flirting!</i>

318
00:21:40,758 --> 00:21:41,801
[line disconnects]

319
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:45,721
[indistinct chatter]

320
00:21:52,770 --> 00:21:54,396
Oh, I'll beat you this time!

321
00:21:56,690 --> 00:21:58,943
[Satoshi] Your face is spinning around.

322
00:21:59,026 --> 00:22:01,821
[Kubocchi] I told you
not to let him drink so much.

323
00:22:01,904 --> 00:22:05,616
-Because you were so pushy.
-[Kubocchi] Please stop that!

324
00:22:05,699 --> 00:22:07,701
[Hikasa] If you can't drink, just say so.

325
00:22:07,785 --> 00:22:09,787
I'm okay! [chuckles]

326
00:22:10,287 --> 00:22:11,705
[Nakazono] Well, he seems good.

327
00:22:11,789 --> 00:22:13,040
[Kubocchi] Are you all right?

328
00:22:13,123 --> 00:22:14,625
I'm sorry.

329
00:22:15,543 --> 00:22:18,170
[Kubocchi] Yanagawa-kun... [echoing]

330
00:22:20,631 --> 00:22:22,967
Are you all right? [echoing]

331
00:22:26,929 --> 00:22:29,932
-[indistinct chatter]
-[birds chirping]

332
00:23:00,254 --> 00:23:01,422
No way.

333
00:23:02,256 --> 00:23:04,675
[♪ comical music playing]

334
00:23:07,553 --> 00:23:09,179
[indistinct chatter]

335
00:23:28,824 --> 00:23:31,660
[whimpering] What the heck?

336
00:23:33,037 --> 00:23:37,958
OSAKA'S TOP FOOD PICK
MENCHIKATSU (DEEP-FRIED MEAT CUTLET)

337
00:23:38,042 --> 00:23:40,044
[♪ light music playing]

338
00:23:40,794 --> 00:23:42,296
[sizzling]

339
00:23:46,383 --> 00:23:47,801
[seller] Here you go.

340
00:23:48,594 --> 00:23:49,720
[crunches]

341
00:23:49,803 --> 00:23:50,971
It's hot!

342
00:23:57,937 --> 00:24:02,858
KAKUZAKI BUTCHER SHOP

343
00:24:02,942 --> 00:24:05,361
[♪ closing theme music playing]
